						}
					]
				},
				{
					"id": "tcJhT13aVGWsLZjjc",
					"name": "Chitin (Hive Tyrant)",
					"reference": "B46",
					"local_notes": "DR 150, all locations (user direction: tougher; was 120), level with the Carnifex. Weak Points 4 (a synapse lord's plating is thicker and better-grown than a rank-and-file predator's): on a hit that fails to penetrate, roll 3d; 4 or less halves DR (75).\n\nLore: A Tyranid's exoskeleton is grown, not worn: dense bio-ceramic chitin fused directly to the flesh beneath it, thickest on the largest bioforms and thin enough on a Termagant to be more like a swarm-trooper's flak jacket than real armour plate. Universal across Codex background and every piece of Black Library Tyranid fiction.\n\nDesign: Damage Resistance (B46, 5/level, all locations): natural DR bought directly on the body, per framework.md's explicit instruction that chitin is a character trait, not equipment. Each body-type lens overrides `levels`/`dr` to its own figure from framework.md's Tyranid anchor table; see that lens's own copy of this trait for its point cost.",
					"tags": [
						"Advantage",
						"Physical",
						"Xenos",
						"Tyranids"
					],
					"points_per_level": 5,
					"can_level": true,
					"levels": 150,
					"features": [
						{
							"type": "dr_bonus",
							"locations": [
								"all"
							],
							"amount": 150
						}
					]
				},
				{
					"id": "tvN67UdVPZMt0TISs",
					"name": "Regeneration (Adapted Biomass)",
					"reference": "B80",
					"local_notes": "Regeneration (Regular): recovers 1 HP per hour even without rest or first aid.\n\nLore: Larger Tyranid bioforms visibly close wounds and regrow damaged tissue over the course of a battle, part of the same adaptive biology that lets the Hive Fleet field bioforms built to take punishment no unaugmented creature could survive. Codex background across editions gives this trait explicitly to Tyranid monstrous creatures.\n\nDesign: Basic Set Regeneration (Regular) (B80, 25 points).",
					"tags": [
						"Advantage",
						"Physical",
						"Xenos",
						"Tyranids"
					],
					"base_points": 25
				},
				{
					"id": "tnL2jRqCzTmp8vFo5",
					"name": "High Pain Threshold",
					"reference": "B59",
					"local_notes": "No shock penalties; +3 to HT rolls to avoid knockdown and stunning.\n\nLore: The synapse lord is the swarm's \"no pain\"; it feels its wounds no more than its brood does.\n\nDesign: Basic Set High Pain Threshold (B59), 10 points (user direction, tougher).",
					"tags": [
						"Advantage",
						"Physical",
						"Xenos",
						"Tyranids"
					],
					"base_points": 10
				},
				{
					"id": "tqJWesBXEbJYgrJ3p",
					"name": "Wings (Flight)",
					"reference": "B56",
					"local_notes": "Disabled by default; enable for a winged Hive Tyrant variant. Air Move equals twice Basic Speed (dropping fractions), per Basic's Flight rule; Winged flight cannot hover and is grounded by high winds or a damaged wing, same as any other winged flier.\n\nLore: Some Hive Tyrants are grown with a huge, membranous wing pair for genuine flight rather than the leaping glides other large bioforms manage — a well-known wargear/bioform option across Codex editions and a striking image in Black Library's Hive Fleet material whenever a Winged Hive Tyrant appears.\n\nDesign: Basic Set Flight (B56, 40 points) with the Winged limitation (-25%, B56, cannot hover, grounded by bad weather or wing damage): 40 x 0.75 = 30 points.",
					"tags": [
						"Advantage",
						"Physical",
						"Xenos",
						"Tyranids"
					],
					"modifiers": [
						{
							"id": "m7_0xv0R13WOQ_QmB",
							"name": "Winged",
							"reference": "B56",
							"cost_adj": "-25%"
						}
					],
					"base_points": 40,
					"disabled": true
				},
				{
					"id": "tKiPpjJ5-EwzHw7A-",
					"name": "Synapse Creature (Hive Tyrant)",
					"reference": "B35",
					"local_notes": "As the Tyranid Warrior's Synapse Creature trait, but out to 32 yards: every friendly Tyranid organism in range gains Synapse Discipline and has Synapse Dependence suppressed while this Hive Tyrant is alive, conscious, and linked to the Hive Mind.\n\nLore: A Hive Tyrant is the Hive Mind's on-the-ground synapse lord: Codex background across editions gives it by far the largest synapse range of any single bioform, able to hold an entire local swarm together where a lone Warrior only holds a squad.\n\nDesign: Affliction (B35) base 10; Advantage Delivered (+10%); Area Effect at the 32-yard tier (+250%, B102); Always On (-40%); Emanation (-20%). Net: +10+250-40-20 = +200%. 10 x 3.0 = 30 points.",
					"tags": [
						"Advantage",
						"Mental",
						"Xenos",
						"Tyranids"
					],
					"modifiers": [
						{
							"id": "mphq3gkQ7jioP63ID",
							"name": "Advantage Delivered (grants Synapse Discipline, 10 pts)",
							"cost_adj": "10%"
						},
						{
							"id": "mgcu1R9nyGsUq7-jg",
							"name": "Area Effect, 32 yards",
							"cost_adj": "+250%"
						},
						{
							"id": "mpyRZwMsgjcnixglX",
							"name": "Always On",
							"cost_adj": "-40%"
						},
						{
							"id": "mOtUG7N9LItsiqBNf",
							"name": "Emanation",
							"cost_adj": "-20%"
						}
					],
					"base_points": 10
				},
				{
					"id": "tcNOsgABAVkNg2oS5",
					"name": "Shadow in the Warp (Hive Tyrant)",
					"reference": "B35",
					"local_notes": "Any psyker within 32 yards suffers -3 to Psyniscience, Warp Sorcery-tagged skill rolls, and the Will roll to resist Perils of the Warp, and must make an immediate Fright Check the first time they come within range.\n\nLore: A Hive Tyrant carries the largest single share of the Hive Mind's psychic mass of any bioform on the ground, matching its synapse range with the widest Shadow in the Warp in this file.\n\nDesign: Affliction (B35) base 10; Disadvantage Delivered (+30%); Area Effect at the 32-yard tier (+250%, B102); Always On (-40%); Emanation (-20%); Accessibility (-20%). Net: +30+250-40-20-20 = +200%. 10 x 3.0 = 30 points.",
					"tags": [
						"Advantage",
						"Mental",
						"Xenos",
						"Tyranids"
					],
					"modifiers": [
						{
							"id": "mW0sQYPLDljPdSA1p",
							"name": "Disadvantage Delivered (Warp-Deafened: -3 to psychic skill and Warp Empowerment-related rolls, plus an immediate Fright Check on first exposure, -30 pts)",
							"cost_adj": "30%"
						},
						{
							"id": "mZxO4YcBaOn1-axEq",
							"name": "Area Effect, 32 yards",
							"cost_adj": "+250%"
						},
						{
							"id": "mUR1vGbVwEakmxm-5",
							"name": "Always On",
							"cost_adj": "-40%"
						},
						{
							"id": "mj4kvZN9UfRD-uQld",
							"name": "Emanation",
							"cost_adj": "-20%"
						},
						{
							"id": "mSBTf_2bl4X-wPblk",
							"name": "Accessibility (only affects psykers and other warp-sensitive minds)",
							"cost_adj": "-20%"
						}
					],
					"base_points": 10
				},
				{
					"id": "tKjhbMKwoaShTXucy",
					"name": "Injury Tolerance (Damage Reduction)",
					"reference": "P53",
					"local_notes": "Divisor 3 (level = divisor): after DR and wounding multipliers, all injury is divided by 3 (round down, minimum 1 if anything penetrated).\n\nLore: A Hive Tyrant's vast bulk and redundant organs make a killing wound very hard to land. Large synapse-beasts and monsters shrug off wounds that would fell smaller creatures.\n\nDesign: Injury Tolerance (Damage Reduction) (GURPS Powers p. 53, 25 points per level, level = divisor): divisor 3 = 75 points. Gives the Hive Tyrant the bulk-and-redundant-organs toughness the lore describes on top of its chitin DR and extra HP.",
					"tags": [
						"Advantage",
						"Physical",
						"Xenos",
						"Tyranids"
					],
					"points_per_level": 25,
					"can_level": true,
					"levels": 3,
					"base_points": 0
				}
			]
		},
		{
			"id": "ttQnie7gEzTweYtxy",
			"name": "Unusual Background (Latent Psychic Potential)",
			"reference": "B96",
			"local_notes": "Lore: Psychic ability is a random, rare mutation of the human genome that lets its bearer perceive and touch the immaterium (the warp). Sources disagree on exact frequency — Imperial administrative texts and Dark Heresy-line background both describe it as \"rare but not vanishingly so,\" on the order of a handful of latent potentials per hive-sized population, with usably strong psykers far rarer still. Treat any precise ratio as flavour, not census data.\n\nDesign: Required to take Psyker (Talent), Warp Empowerment, or any trait carrying the Warp Sorcery power modifier below. Unusual Background (B96) leaves its cost to the GM; 10 points reflects that the ability itself is not learned but grants access to an entire framework of further abilities, roughly the going rate other published settings use for \"you may buy from this power list at all.\"",
			"tags": [
				"Advantage",
				"Mental",
				"Psyker",
				"Imperium"
			],
			"base_points": 10
		},
		{
			"id": "tRnIv9tedlD5-TaGf",
			"name": "Warp Empowerment",
			"reference": "TSOR4",
			"local_notes": "A direct reskin of Sorcerous Empowerment (Thaumatology: Sorcery, TSOR4):\nthe psyker's raw, trained capacity to draw on and shape the warp, as\ndistinct from Psyker (Talent, TSOR5's Sorcery Talent analogue, below)\nwhich only sharpens related skills. Requires Unusual Background (Latent\nPsychic Potential). It is the prerequisite for every Warp Sorcery-tagged\nability in this file (see Witch-sight and each discipline below); the\nNavigator's Third Eye and the Pariah/Untouchable genes carry no Warp\nSorcery modifier and so need no Warp Empowerment.\n\nCap, cast per Thaumatology: Sorcery (TSOR): a psyker may only know a\npower whose full, modified point cost is no greater than the point cost\nof their own Warp Empowerment (10 + 10/level). A power bought at a\nhigher level (more dice, more range, etc.) costs proportionally more and\nmay outgrow a psyker's Empowerment even after they first learned it at a\ncheaper level — raising the level, and cost, of Warp Empowerment is how\na psyker \"grows into\" costlier or higher-level workings.\n\nImperial Assignment scale (Adeptus Astra Telepathica / Black Ships)\nmapped to Warp Empowerment level and the point cap that gives, worked\nout from this file's actual (Warp Sorcery -20% + Perils of the Warp)\nmodified costs. Attack powers are bought at lore levels (Smite and\nMolten Beam 12 levels at 162 points, Inferno 68, Crush 88, Fire Bolt\n42, Flame Breath 30, Assail 28), so only a strong psyker can hold one\nat full strength; a weaker one buys the same power at fewer levels\n(cost is per level: Smite and Molten Beam 13.5, Inferno 8.5, Crush 11,\nFlame Breath 6, Fire Bolt and Assail 3.5).\n\n  Grade      | Empowerment level | Cap (10+10/lvl) | What the cap reaches\n  Iota       | 1                  | 20              | every non-attack power costing 20 or less: Endurance (2), Iron Arm (4), Warp Speed (4), Forewarning (11), Psychic Scream (12), Heroic Feats of Strength (12), Sanctuary (13), Mind Probe (14), Foresight (18), Misfortune (18), Haemorrhage (19), Astrotelepathy (20). Attack powers only at reduced levels: Smite 1 level, Fire Bolt or Assail up to 5 levels, Crush 1 level\n  Zeta       | 1                  | 20              | as Iota; low Psyker Talent limits skill use, not what they can know\n  Eta        | 2                  | 30              | adds Mental Interrogation (21), Null Zone (23), Terrify (28), Assail at full (28), Flame Breath at full (30). Smite 2 levels, Fire Bolt 8 levels, Crush 2 levels\n  Theta      | 3                  | 40              | adds Scrier's Gaze (35), Dominate (35), Gate of Infinity (40): the full non-attack roster. Fire Bolt 11 levels, Crush 3 levels, Smite 2 levels\n  Epsilon    | 5                  | 60              | Fire Bolt at full (42) with Flame Breath (30) and Assail (28) at full (a typical Wyrdvane battlefield psyker); Smite, Molten Beam or Crush at 4-5 levels\n  Delta      | 16                 | 170             | Smite and Molten Beam at full 12 levels (162), Inferno at full (68), Crush at full (88): the whole Imperial attack roster (a typical Sanctioned Primaris Psyker)\n  Gamma      | 16                 | 170             | as Delta, better skills from a higher Psyker Talent\n  Beta       | 18                 | 190             | as Delta with headroom to push one attack to 14 levels (189)\n  Alpha      | 20                 | 210             | full roster with headroom for high-level workings, up to 15 levels of Smite or Molten Beam (203) (Astartes Librarians, Black Ship candidates)\n  Alpha-Plus | 25+ (GM only)      | 260+            | 19 levels of Smite (257) and beyond; Vortex of Doom (280 as usually bought) needs level 27, so it stays just out of reach here\n\nA character need not buy Warp Empowerment up to their grade's full\nceiling: templates in this project buy only the level their actually-\nknown powers need, and note the grade's theoretical ceiling separately.\n\nLore: The Iota-to-Alpha-Plus assignment scale is drawn from the Adeptus Astra Telepathica's own grading of psychic potential as depicted across Dark Heresy-line material and repeated in Codex/Imperial Armour background; Black Library uses the same grades in passing (e.g. Eisenhorn-cycle and Ciaphas Cain references to Alpha-class talents). \"Alpha-Plus\" specifically denotes the rarest, most dangerous talents the Black Ships process. Only the Alpha/Beta/Gamma end of that ordering is well attested outside the RPG lines; the full Iota-to-Theta ordering used in the table above is Dark Heresy-line material and is not confirmed by the fiction.\n\nDesign: Sorcerous Empowerment (TSOR4) costs 10 base + 10/level (level 1 = 20 points, each further level +10) in the GCS master Thaumatology data; reused verbatim here under a 40k-appropriate name, since the underlying mechanic — \"how much warp-power you can channel at all, gating which spells/powers you may know by their modified cost\" — is exactly what an Imperial Assignment grade represents. The level-to-grade mapping above is derived, not asserted: it walks every power in this file's actual modified cost (recomputed under the new Warp Sorcery -20% modifier, see below) and finds the cheapest Empowerment level whose cap clears it, so \"Iota can only cast minor powers at full strength\" and \"Alpha can hold every attack power at full lore strength with room to spare\" are literally true of the numbers, not just flavour text. Levels were raised well past the old 1-7 range because attack powers now cost 162 points at lore scale rather than a handful.",
			"tags": [
				"Advantage",
				"Mental",
				"Talent",
				"Psyker",
				"Imperium"
			],
			"points_per_level": 10,
			"can_level": true,
			"levels": 2,
			"base_points": 10
		},
		{
			"id": "t_HpFOj4cNSSf3k0X",
			"name": "Psyker",
			"reference": "TSOR5",
			"local_notes": "This project's Sorcery Talent (Thaumatology: Sorcery, TSOR5) analogue:\napplies as Sorcery Talent applies to a sorcerer's skills in TSOR, just\nto a 40k-specific list — Psyniscience, Meditation, Hidden Lore (the\nWarp), and the Will roll to resist Perils of the Warp (see above) — a\nhouse extension of Talent's normal \"add to listed skills\" rule,\nprecedented by Magery's and Sorcery Talent's own habit of aiding\nrelated rolls beyond pure spellcasting. Reaction bonus: +1/level from\nother sanctioned psykers and the Astra Telepathica.\n\nPsyker (Talent) and Warp Empowerment are separate purchases on separate\naxes, exactly as Sorcery Talent and Sorcerous Empowerment are in TSOR:\nthis trait only sharpens related skills and Perils resistance, while\nWarp Empowerment (above) is what actually gates which powers a psyker\nmay know. A high-Talent, low-Empowerment psyker is a sharp, well-drilled\nmind who simply hasn't learned much yet; the reverse is a raw prodigy\nwho is clumsy with the skills around their gift.\n\nImperial Assignment scale (Adeptus Astra Telepathica / Black Ships),\nweakest to strongest, mapped to Talent level. See Warp Empowerment above\nfor the matching Empowerment level/point-cap column, which is the real\ngate on ability selection:\n  Iota    — Talent 0 (latent; register but rarely take Psyker traits at all)\n  Zeta    — Talent 1\n  Eta     — Talent 1\n  Theta   — Talent 2\n  Epsilon — Talent 2  (typical Wyrdvane conscript)\n  Delta   — Talent 3  (typical Sanctioned Primaris Psyker)\n  Gamma   — Talent 4\n  Beta    — Talent 4  (many Astropaths)\n  Alpha   — Talent 5  (Astartes Librarians, Black Ship candidates)\n  Alpha-Plus — Talent 6+ (beyond-play tier: Primarchs,\n    the most powerful Inquisitors, the worst Chaos sorcerers)\n\nLore: The Iota-to-Alpha-Plus assignment scale is drawn from the Adeptus Astra Telepathica's own grading of psychic potential as depicted across Dark Heresy-line material and repeated in Codex/Imperial Armour background; Black Library uses the same grades in passing (e.g. Eisenhorn-cycle and Ciaphas Cain references to Alpha-class talents). \"Alpha-Plus\" specifically denotes the rarest, most dangerous talents the Black Ships process. Grade names beyond Alpha/Beta/Gamma are RPG-line material only.\n\nDesign: Talent affecting four things (three skills plus the Perils resistance roll) sits at Basic's \"Medium Talent\" rate of 10 points/level (B90, three-to-five-skill bracket) rather than 5 (one-two skills) or 15 (six-nine skills) — the same rate Sorcery Talent itself uses (TSOR5, 10/level). Capped at level 6 for player characters; higher grades are GM-reference only, per the framework's \"Beyond play\" tier.",
			"tags": [
				"Advantage",
				"Mental",
				"Talent",
				"Psyker",
				"Imperium"
			],
			"points_per_level": 10,
			"can_level": true,
			"levels": 3,
			"base_points": 0,
			"max_levels": 6
		},
		{
			"id": "t5Xebo2Rcbkvo5ckQ",
			"name": "The Horror",
			"local_notes": "Lore: A wave of pure, alien wrongness projected directly into a target's mind, distinct from Shadow in the Warp's constant background hum — a focused psychic terror-strike the Hive Mind can direct at a single dangerous enemy (an officer, a Librarian) rather than merely radiating outward. Consistent with Codex background's framing of the Hive Mind as capable of directed as well as ambient psychic effects.\n\nDesign: Terror, Basic's core advantage (flat 30 + 10/level for extra range, B), with Warp Sorcery/Perils, net -30%, identical build to this project's own Telepathy: Terrify entry. Full modified cost: (30+10) x 0.7 = 28 points at its default first extra-range level; needs Warp Empowerment level 2 (cap 30).",
			"tags": [
				"Advantage",
				"Mental",
				"Xenos",
				"Tyranids"
			],
			"modifiers": [
				{
					"id": "mYYy9nRy8Vc0nTA6u",
					"name": "Warp Sorcery",
					"cost_adj": "-20%"
				},
				{
					"id": "m8C1nPbkdmicMWRPO",
					"name": "Perils of the Warp",
					"cost_adj": "-10%"
				}
			],
			"points_per_level": 10,
			"can_level": true,
			"levels": 1,
			"base_points": 30
		},
		{
			"id": "t8jsodJX994d1Zh5-",
			"name": "Dominion",
			"local_notes": "Lore: A Hive Tyrant's own signature working: it reaches into a target with the same crushing psychic weight it uses to hold its own swarm together, stripping away whatever protects them and leaving them more vulnerable to everything that follows — Codex background names this kind of debuff among a synapse lord's psychic gifts, and this project's own reasoned scaling of it onto the Hive Mind's known telepathic dominance theme, on the model of this project's Librarius: Null Zone (the closest published analogue for \"strip an enemy's defences from a distance\").\n\nDesign: Affliction (10/level) delivering a Vulnerability-style disadvantage valued at roughly -20 points (+20%, matching this project's own Null Zone valuation), Malediction (+100%, B36), Warp Sorcery and the Severe Perils tier (a Hive Tyrant-scale psychic push, matching Null Zone's own Severe tier), net +80%. Full modified cost: 10 x 1.8 = 18 points/level; needs Warp Empowerment level 2 (cap 30).",
			"tags": [
				"Advantage",
				"Mental",
				"Xenos",
				"Tyranids"
			],
			"modifiers": [
				{
					"id": "mJsZg5Uo5YkCPZLv1",
					"name": "Disadvantage Delivered (Vulnerability x1.5, -20 pts)",
					"cost_adj": "20%"
				},
				{
					"id": "mLc2q53m474-F8-kL",
					"name": "Malediction 1",
					"cost_adj": "+100%"
				},
				{
					"id": "mWyhlzeFx8JAburBg",
					"name": "Warp Sorcery",
					"cost_adj": "-20%"
				},
				{
					"id": "mLhO7NuznTiWF6SPx",
					"name": "Perils of the Warp (Severe)",
					"cost_adj": "-20%"
				}
			],
			"points_per_level": 10,
			"can_level": true,
			"levels": 1
		},
		{
			"id": "t9ZnGqIOcO2TO70ku",
			"name": "Monstrous Scything Talons",
			"reference": "B88",
			"local_notes": "Lore: Scything talons grown to Carnifex or Hive Tyrant scale: blades the size of a man, capable of shearing clean through a light vehicle's hull as easily as a Marine's plate. Codex: Tyranids background treats monstrous scything talons as one of the Carnifex's signature close-combat options, a genuine threat to armour that would shrug off a Warrior's own scything talons entirely.\n\nDesign: Framework.md's own anchor: \"Monstrous scything talons | sw+4d(3) cut.\" Built at a Carnifex's own ST 60 (sw 9d): Cutting Striker (B88, 7 points) with Armor Divisor (3) (+100%) = 14 for the sw+0(3) baseline; the anchor's own +4d is bought as Innate Attack (Cut) (B61, 7/die) at 4 dice = 28, with Armor Divisor (3) (+100%) and Melee Attack, Reach C (-30%): net +70%, 28x1.7=47.6, rounded to 48. Total 14+48=62. Checked by exact dice distribution at ST 60 (sw+4d(3) = 13d(3)): averages 45.5 and penetrates Astartes plate (DR 100, eff. 33.3) 97.5% of the time, Gravis (DR 130) 62.6%, and a Terminator (DR 200, eff. 66.7) 0%. A Hive Tyrant at ST 55 (12d+1(3), average 43) gets 94.6% against Astartes plate, 46.7% against Gravis and 0% against a Terminator. Against vehicles at ST 60: AV10 74.0%, AV11 0.4%, AV12 and up 0%. That is a decisive Marine-killer and a light-vehicle cracker, but not a Terminator-killer: the crushing claws below are the swarm's armour-buster.",
			"tags": [
				"Advantage",
				"Physical",
				"Xenos",
				"Tyranids"
			],
			"base_points": 62,
			"weapons": [
				{
					"id": "wgmwJHbS0c_6UL0az",
					"sv": 1,
					"damage": {
						"type": "cut",
						"st": "sw",
						"base": "4d",
						"armor_divisor": 3
					},
					"reach": "1,2",
					"parry": "0",
					"usage": "Standard",
					"usage_notes": "Written for a Carnifex-scale bearer (ST 60, sw 9d, giving a total of 13d(3) cut); a Hive Tyrant (ST 55, sw 8d+1) totals 12d+1(3). Rebuild the +4d Innate Attack component for any other bearer's own ST per this file's header note.",
					"defaults": [
						{
							"type": "dx",
							"modifier": 0
						},
						{
							"type": "skill",
